1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
On the frontier, after a night of fierce wind, the old man’s fine horse crossed the pass and was gone.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,500
Father, the post is still here. The rope has snapped.

3
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:10,500
To lose such a splendid horse—old brother, that is a great misfortune.

4
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:13,000
How can we know this will not turn out to be a blessing?

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
The others saw only emptiness, but the old man would not write that emptiness as final.

6
00:00:15,093 --> 00:00:18,093
Months later, the north wind changed direction, and the old hoofprints brought back new hoofbeats.

7
00:00:18,093 --> 00:00:21,593
Fate led the dust, and at first said nothing.

8
00:00:22,093 --> 00:00:26,093
One horse has brought back so many—old brother, this time it is great good fortune!

9
00:00:26,093 --> 00:00:30,093
How can we know this will not turn out to be a misfortune?

10
00:00:30,162 --> 00:00:33,162
Father, this horse knows the wind!

11
00:00:39,162 --> 00:00:42,162
How has such good fortune come to this?

12
00:00:42,162 --> 00:00:45,162
How can we know this will not turn out to be a blessing?

13
00:00:45,231 --> 00:00:47,231
Before long, Hu soldiers invaded deep into the frontier, and all the young men of the village were conscripted to the pass.

14
00:00:47,231 --> 00:00:51,231
Those whose names are on the list, go north.

15
00:00:51,231 --> 00:00:55,731
Lame leg. Stay.

16
00:00:55,731 --> 00:01:00,231
And so fortune and misfortune lean upon one another; even the rope that ties a horse may one day bind a life to safety.
